NAME
       vainfo - display information from the VA-API driver

SYNOPSIS
       vainfo [--display drm|x11] [--device path] [-a]

DESCRIPTION
       This program displays information about the VA-API (video acceleration)
       driver  installed  in  the  system:  the library version, the driver it
       loaded and every profile and entrypoint (decode, encode, video process-
       ing) the driver offers for the graphics device.

OPTIONS
       --display drm|x11
              The back end to open the device through.  drm opens  the  render
              node  directly  and  needs  no  X server; x11 asks the running X
              server for the device.  Without the option the X11 back  end  is
              tried when DISPLAY is set, the DRM one otherwise.

       --device path
              The render node for the DRM back end, /dev/dri/renderD128 by de-
              fault.

       -a, --all
              Print every attribute of every configuration as well.

ENVIRONMENT
       LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME
              The  driver to load in place of the one chosen from the graphics
              device's kernel driver (for Intel graphics: iHD, then i965).

       LIBVA_DRIVERS_PATH
              Where the drivers are looked for, /usr/lib/dri by default.

SEE ALSO
       ffmpeg(1), gst-inspect-1.0(1), drminfo(1)

